# Copy to `.env` to override the backend the app talks to during local dev
# (`npm start` / `expo start`). Expo's CLI auto-loads `.env` from this
# directory — no extra tooling needed.
#
# Leave unset (or delete .env) to fall back to your own machine: the app then
# auto-detects your Expo dev server's LAN IP and talks to a backend running
# locally on port 3001. See src/api/client.ts's resolveApiUrl().
#
# EAS cloud builds don't read this file — `eas.json`'s build.preview.env and
# build.production.env already hardcode the deployed Render URL for those.

# API_URL=https://dyp-farms-api.onrender.com/api
